From: Ferdous Bhai <ferdousbd@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:21:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20optional=20Padm=C3=A9=20padding=20for?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20pack=20files?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a `pack_padding` repository config option (`--set-pack-padding`), off
by default. When on, each pack gets one random, unreferenced data blob
before its header is written, sized so the finished pack is exactly a
Padmé size. Small packs then no longer reveal the exact size of the file
they hold; the overhead is at most 12%.

The padding blob is an ordinary indexed blob (id = hash of its
plaintext), so padded packs stay valid restic packs. Prune drops padding
as unused data on repack; the repacker carries the setting, so repacked
packs are padded again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
